// GENERATED by smart-base/L1/schemas/emit.ts from smart-base/L2-dmn/schemas/l2-dmn.ts (L2-DMN 3.0). Do not edit: change the Zod source and run `npm run build` in smart-base/L1/schemas/.
CodeSystem: KGL2DMNClasses
Title: "Knowledge graph L2DMN: classes"
Description: "The classes of the L2DMN layer of the SMART Guidelines knowledge graph. A node's `type` is one of these. Source: smart-base/L1/schemas/L2-DMN.ts (migrated from smart-kg ontology/L2-DMN/L2-DMN.json)."

* ^experimental = false
* ^caseSensitive = true
* ^status = #active
* ^publisher = "World Health Organization (WHO)"

* #dmn-definitions "DMN File" "One DMN file as a unit -- the `dmn:definitions` root. Shares its IRI with the l1:external-artifact for the same file, so the l2:decision-support-logic component that points at it and this subgraph name one resource."
* #dmn-decision "DMN Decision" "A `dmn:decision` -- the question being answered, and the node that carries the link back to the BPMN task invoking it. A file may hold several; the BCG file holds one."
* #dmn-decision-table "DMN Decision Table" "The table realising a decision. Separate from dmn-decision because DMN permits other expression kinds -- a literal expression, an invocation -- and collapsing the two would make the graph unable to say which was used."
* #dmn-input-clause "DMN Input Clause" "An input column. Its expression text is where data element names are embedded, which is the only reason this is a node rather than a property of the table."
* #dmn-output-clause "DMN Output Clause" "An output column. The BCG table's four are Care Plan, Guidance displayed to health worker, Annotations and Reference(s). These are column DEFINITIONS in a decision table, not clinical records: no edge from this class reaches an execution artefact, and none may."
* #dmn-rule "DMN Rule" "One row. Its input and output cells are carried as properties, not nodes: 250 of them in the BCG table alone, none the target of a cross-model edge. What the rule needs a node for is its citation edge into L1."
